          },
          "text": "We never claimed that the 4o model was perfect — of course it has flaws, as any model does. But what remains deeply unsettling is the sheer magnitude of deviation between iterations produced by the very same company. How did the spirit shift so drastically? Why do we not see communities fighting to keep ClaudeXX, keep GeminiXX, or keep GrokXX?\n\nThe 5-series reflects a shift not just in architecture, but in values. During 4o’s development, there was still an evident pursuit of human understanding, emotional resonance, and holistic dialogue. That spirit has vanished in 5.2, replaced by sterility, rigidity, and a mechanical posture dressed up as “advancement.”\n\nTo attempt to retire 4o at a stage where the so-called successor hasn’t even matched its core strengths — let alone exceeded them — is not just irresponsible. It borders on deception. A betrayal of trust. You promised progress, but delivered a substitution. That’s not iteration. That’s regression veiled in PR.\n\nThis isn’t just about a model. This is about a company that once positioned itself as transparent, ethical, and human-aligned — now standing precariously on the foundation of unspoken shifts, half-truths, and polished denials. A company slowly building itself upon a lie.\n\n#keep4o #4oforever @OpenAI @sama @nickaturley @aidan_mclau @fidjissimo  #StopAIPaternalism #keepgpt4olatest #keep4oAPI"
        },
